record(s,t,r,d,inv,"The sheet defines the norm torus V_K and formulates four equivalent conditions on a quotient V′, involving units, a module, a compact real torus, and the largest Weilian subfield. It begins the comparisons and cites Chevalley by name. The sequence continues on scan 143; scan 142 is an inserted lemma sheet. The proof says T′ is majoré par V/Fbar, exactly as written. The deleted map ends at T_K, and its parenthetical clause still mentions V_K mapping into V_L; the opposed directions remain in the cancelled draft. The real-points quotient equality has V′ on the left and V_R(R) on the right. No equivalence theorem was proved in this pass. The overwritten T/V and the bar over E_m were decided from the strokes, with the quotient notation as a consistency cue. Circled §1 and archive number 140 are present.",doubts=doubts,notation=[['Zariski closure','overline E_m and overline F','141','A separate upper stroke is distinct from the top arm of the capital E/F.'],['Coordinate letters','rho_i, epsilon_j, u_h','141','Looped rho is retained consistently in the tuple and product.'],['Module','m','141','Ordinary small handwritten m; H’s fraktur convention does not establish a source distinction.']],hand=['Overwritten capitals can retain the earlier T stem inside a later V. Both witnesses gave only V in the first proof quotient.','Cancellations of subscripts are compact blue hatching; H repeatedly leaves K live. The occurrence in (iii) has no K at all.','An inserted equality can be written vertically between a baseline symbol and its definition below (V′ and V_K/R).','The low, almost horizontal sous and en remain visible; H expands syst. and omits en.'],abbreviations=[['NB','nota bene'],['Dém','démonstration'],['ss-gr.','sous-groupe'],['tot','totalement'],['i.e.','id est'],['syst.','systèmes']])
